Shearing and stretching the figure (an affine map) keeps parallel lines parallel, midpoints as midpoints, and all area ratios. So we may take $ABCD$ to be a rectangle with $AD = 2AB$: then $ABNM$ and $MNCD$ are squares, each of area $96$.

The triangle $POQ$ is made of four pieces:
* the square $ABNM$: $96$;
* triangle $NBP \cong NCD$: half of square $MNCD$, i.e. $48$;
* triangle $MAQ\cong MDC$: also $48$;
* triangle $MNO$: a quarter of square $MNCD$ ($O$ is its centre), i.e. $24$.

Total $96+48+48+24=216$.

**Answer: 216**
